parts.text:
We need implement new welcome block centered vertically and horizontally in results area. Reuse SVG from index.html with all letters and dots exactly #2E1C74. Don't change white logo. No images/hexagons/boxes/backgrounds. Behavior current.

Need decide markup. The results panel `.viewWindow-panel-container` currently has padding-top 30 (desktop) and bottom 70, plus other content. To center welcome in results area vertically, easiest CSS: make welcome block absolute or flex? We need not disturb existing results when a sequence selected. Add class `.sequencia-boas-vindas` inside results container. For no selection, it should occupy results area and center. Could style:
```
<div id="results" class="...">
  <div class="viewWindow-panel-container">
    <div class="sequencia-boas-vindas" ng-show="...">
      <div class="sequencia-boas-vindas-conteudo">
        <p class="sequencia-boas-vindas-saudacao">Bem-vindo ao</p>
        <div class="sequencia-logo">
          svg...
        </div>
        <p class="sequencia-boas-vindas-instrucao">Escolha...</p>
      </div>
    </div>
...
```
Need center block vertically/horizontally of results area. Since the container has padding and results panel fixed height desktop. We could set `.sequencia-boas-vindas` height to fill available panel area and use flex center. But `.viewWindow-panel-container` is inside panel; padding-top 30, padding-bottom 70, and there are sibling elements (selected div, row). When no selection, the selected div is `ng-hide` and row has no music (height 0) but still `.row`. The welcome could be:
```
.sequencia-boas-vindas {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-height: calc(100vh - 160px); /* desktop results panel height calc(100vh - 70px) minus padding */
  text-align: center;
